hangul-syllables.tsv — Korean syllable frequency model for KeyHue's experimental
"Warn When Typing in the Wrong Language" feature (docs/adr/0041).

This file is NOT covered by KeyHue's MIT License.

It contains syllable and syllable-pair counts derived from the text of the
Korean Wikipedia (https://ko.wikipedia.org), dump kowiki-20260901,
pages-articles1 (articles p1–p82407), by scripts/build-mistype-model.sh.

Source text: Korean Wikipedia contributors, licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0).

Changes: the article text was stripped of wiki markup, split into words made
only of Hangul syllables, and reduced to counts of single syllables and adjacent
syllable pairs. No sentences or words are included.

